      },
      "lineNbr": 95,
      "author": {
        "id": 1588887
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-01T14:20:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I needed to added `zephyr,deferred-init` to `pwrmon` and PACs, that\u0027s why I do `device_init` on PACS  inside  `pwrmon_init`. `pwrmon_init` is called when `PWRMON_START` is issued.",
      "parentUuid": "9dc83857_311eae22",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 95,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "a405444314a2cc5767a76de98a34fe33ca6c27ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9081e95f_395644bc",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/pwrmon/pwrmon.c",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 95,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-12T19:07:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now `pwrmon_init` is called automatically when the EC boots.  You can set the `init` routine on `DEVICE_DT_INST_DEFINE` to NULL, and then just call `pwrmon_init` only after the host sends `EC_PWRMON_START`.  \n\nYou should add a guard so that the `device_init()` is only called once, and only need to check that the GPIO is ready once.\n\nIt should be okay to call `gpio_pin_configure_dt` everytime the host sends `EC_PWRMON_START`.",
      "parentUuid": "cc02a140_2c22fa59",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 95,
        "endChar": 47
      },
