      "writtenOn": "2026-05-28T15:14:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "hey just to followup on the sync up meeting we had, have you had a chance to consider MKBP for the actual data streaming? it\u0027d be way easier to do it now than switch to that later",
      "revId": "a405444314a2cc5767a76de98a34fe33ca6c27ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b19f161_9675e617",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/pwrmon/pwrmon.c",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 333,
      "author": {
        "id": 1588887
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T12:59:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have stable kernel driver, MKBP requires modifying kernel driver, it can lead to regression.\n\nHowever, I\u0027 working on sending multiple channels in one `EC_PWRMON_GET` command to reduce overhead.",
      "parentUuid": "bd62fa4a_c126e94d",
      "revId": "a405444314a2cc5767a76de98a34fe33ca6c27ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b679e3f8_b587c3f6",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/pwrmon/pwrmon.c",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 333,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T17:14:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it is still worth investigating whether MKBP can be used here. It this isn\u0027t evaluated now, we\u0027re locked into a potentially inferior solution.",
      "parentUuid": "3b19f161_9675e617",
      "revId": "a405444314a2cc5767a76de98a34fe33ca6c27ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "391237bb_e284e075",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/pwrmon/pwrmon.c",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 333,
      "author": {
        "id": 1588887
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-02T14:14:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did some research what I need to do to convert to MKBP, besides modification to `cros_ec_pwrmon.c` and `pwrmon.c`, I need to modify to common `cros_ec_commands.h`, which is a GKI header. IMO modifying common GKI header is out of reach.\n\nSpeaking about modification, this is what I need to add [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/ec_commands.h;drc\u003dc4ec9ee779756327fd1a4b50f97679c05c493992;l\u003d4270) `struct ec_response_pwrmon_fifo_info` or `struct ec_response_pwrmon_data_fifo`.",
      "parentUuid": "b679e3f8_b587c3f6",
      "revId": "a405444314a2cc5767a76de98a34fe33ca6c27ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08e1bea1_6e8eb367",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/pwrmon/pwrmon.c",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 333,
      "author": {
        "id": 1588887
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-12T15:37:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I made an test with sending multiple channels per one `GET` command:\n\nFor batch of 4 with current upstream version of PAC194X driver, EC needs 6-8 ms to return response, for 8 channel batch around 10-15 ms are needed to send back data.\n\nHowever, If this [PR](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/109415) gets merged, EC needs 3-5 ms for 4 channel batch and 4-7 ms for batch of 8. Additionally this PR will simplify `pwrmon` logic.",
      "parentUuid": "391237bb_e284e075",
      "revId": "a405444314a2cc5767a76de98a34fe33ca6c27ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "397c5704_31b1bac2",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/pwrmon/pwrmon.c",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 333,
      "author": {
        "id": 1478788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-24T14:37:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How much of a problem is the GKI modification? Modifying a header does not sound like a huge deal plus android desktop has the whole system in place to land the change immediately in the downstream repository, it feels like we are taking a shortcut to be honest and the subsystem is using the wrong api at the moment, it\u0027d be nice to get it right from the start rather than changing it down the road.",
